---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title={`About | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="What The Morning Build is, how the daily briefing is made, and how to follow it."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="digest">
      <h1>About {SITE_NAME}</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          {SITE_NAME} is a daily briefing on AI and tech for people who build
          software. Every morning it covers the handful of stories that
          actually matter: what happened, why it matters, and what to watch
          next. The whole thing reads in about two minutes.
        </p>

        <h2>How it's made</h2>
        <p>
          Each morning an automated pipeline reads the day's reporting from
          established tech outlets, including TechCrunch, The Verge, Ars
          Technica, VentureBeat, and Hacker News. It selects the most
          significant stories for an engineering audience and drafts the
          briefing with the help of AI, grounded strictly in the source
          articles. Every story links to its original reporting, so you can
          always go deeper or check the source yourself.
        </p>
        <p>
          The pipeline never invents facts: if the sources don't say it, the
          briefing doesn't either. When a story is thin or the day is quiet,
          the briefing runs shorter rather than padding itself out.
        </p>

        <h2>Follow along</h2>
        <p>
          New briefings publish every morning. Read them here, or subscribe
          via <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a> or <a href="/atom.xml">Atom</a> in
          your feed reader. A daily email edition is planned.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
